      "description": "Watch Luton vs Stockport County highlights and goals from League One on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 2, 2026. The clash between Luton and Stockport County promised a tactical showdown in League One , with both teams eager to secure vital points. On September 2, 2026 , the stadium buzzed with anticipation as these two competitive sides took to the pitch for a crucial league fixture. A Tense and Tactical First Half From the opening whistle, it was clear that neither side was willing to give an inch. The first half was characterized by disciplined defending and a cagey midfield battle, as Luton looked to leverage their home advantage while Stockport County remained compact. Despite several promising build-up plays, clear-cut chances were at a premium. The referee brought the opening period to a close after two minutes of stoppage time, leaving the fans waiting for the breakthrough as the teams headed into the tunnels with the scoreline level. Breaking the Deadlock in the Second Period The second half sparked into life almost immediately. In the 50th minute, the deadlock was finally broken when Nahki Wells found the back of the net, clinical finishing giving Stockport County a precious lead. The momentum of the match shifted as Luton tried to respond, but the game grew increasingly physical. This intensity was reflected in the referee's notebook, with Daniel Gore receiving a yellow card in the 56th minute as the battle for control intensified across the park. Impact Subs and the Final Blow Managerial decisions played a pivotal role in the closing stages. In the 65th minute, goalscorer Nahki Wells made way for Callum Marshall in a triple substitution that refreshed the visitor's frontline. The move paid dividends just eleven minutes later. In the 76th minute, Jamie Donley turned provider, delivering a sharp assist for Callum Marshall to double the lead. Luton pushed forward in the final quarter, introducing the likes of Mikael Mandron and Gideon Kodua to find a way back, but the visitors held firm. Despite a late yellow card for Oliver Norwood , Stockport County managed the game professionally through four minutes of added time to secure a convincing victory on the road."
