      "description": "Watch Stockport County vs Wycombe Wanderers highlights and goals from League One on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 29, 2026. Stockport County and Wycombe Wanderers faced off in a highly anticipated League One fixture on August 29, 2026. Both sides took to the pitch with high intensity, promising a contest filled with tactical shifts and attacking intent. Early Surge at Edgeley Park The home side wasted no time establishing their dominance. In the 16th minute, Lewis Bate turned provider for Harry Wood , who clinicaly finished to give Stockport County the lead. The pressure remained relentless, and by the 23rd minute, the advantage was doubled. Kyle Wootton teed up Harry Wood for his second of the afternoon, leaving the visitors struggling to contain the wave of attacks. Wycombe Wanderers did find a lifeline just before the interval. In the 43rd minute, Cauley Woodrow struck back to reduce the deficit, ensuring the game remained competitive as the teams headed into the tunnel for half-time. Second Half Dominance Any hopes of a Wycombe comeback were swiftly dampened after the restart. In the 56th minute, Kyle Wootton turned from provider to scorer, converting a chance created by Oliver Norwood . The momentum was firmly with the hosts, and only five minutes later, Jack Diamond found the net to further extend the lead to 4-1. A series of tactical changes followed as both managers looked to manage the final stages of the match. Stockport's depth was on full display when substitute Mikael Mandron added a fifth goal in the 90th minute, assisted by Benony Andresson . The final whistle at 90+5' confirmed a comprehensive performance from the home side in front of their jubilant supporters."
